From 93c4defb520a1cc56f2d8c58290b79b0fb170601 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:52:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: checks of the variables declared for some hypotheses
 only

BehaviourDescription::checkVariableExistence returns a pair whose first
member tells if the variable is declared for all the modelling hypotheses
and whose second member tells if it is declared for at least one of them.
Its callers tested them the other way around (`if (first)` then
`!second`), so that their checks never triggered: a variable declared for
some hypotheses only was treated as not declared, and the error came later,
as a conflict of names. The checks of BrickUtilities,
BehaviourBrickBase, HookeStressPotentialBase, IsotropicBehaviourDSLBase,
ImplicitDSLBase and RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase now test that the
variable is declared for at least one hypothesis, then for all of them,
and report it. Missing space fixed in one of their messages.

The code generated for the 757 MFront files of TFEL, MGIS, mfem-mgis and
the examples which mfront accepts is identical; DSLTest checks the new
messages of two partial declarations (and fails with the previous code).
